{
  "reason": "Use Tier 2: replace target-only negative filtering with user-history-aware false-negative filtering in the sampled-softmax objective. Cross-view consistency improved HR@10 from 0.5463 to 0.5575 but remains below 0.5800; further representation alignment has not recovered the best result. The current loss treats other known training interactions as negatives, potentially opposing both recommendation and reconstruction supervision, so correcting this conflict is a distinct, testable hypothesis.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Extend MaskedHistories to provide each example's complete training-history item set solely as negative-exclusion metadata. Use a custom collate function to concatenate unique history IDs with their batch-row indices, avoiding dense batch-by-catalog masks. Preserve existing sequence, labels, auxiliary_sequence, auxiliary_labels, prefix sampling, corruption draws, prediction_sequence, and supplied splits; never use validation interactions for training exclusions or expose this metadata to the encoder. Keep DataLoader workers and seed settings unchanged.",
    "model_design": null,
    "training_evaluation": "Change negative supervision by masking every sampled negative that appears anywhere in the corresponding user's training history, retaining target-collision masking and the existing 256 shared uniform draws. Construct a batch-by-256 exclusion mask from the collated metadata, map auxiliary reconstruction queries to their originating batch rows, and apply identical exclusions to clean and corrupted consistency logits before softmax. Preserve the positive column, supervised loss weights, consistency coefficient, architecture, optimizer, hyperparameters, and checkpoint selection so this is one controlled objective experiment. Verify exclusion alignment and finite losses, including rows with every sampled negative excluded; preserve train_one, evaluate, write_predict_script, and the exported predict signature, checking score parity after strict checkpoint reload. Retain DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four category routes, one newly trained selected checkpoint per category, trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution, and fixed validation HR@10; print the measured macro validation score and leave hidden-test inference to the host."
  }
}
